@@ -1,5 +1,18 @@
 Quickstart
 ==========
 
+Case-Insensitive Header Mappings
+--------------------------------
+
+``CaseInsensitiveDict`` supports mapping union operations. Both operands must
+be mappings:
+
+    >>> merged = response.headers | {"X-Request-ID": "123"}
+    >>> merged = {"X-Request-ID": "123"} | response.headers
+    >>> response.headers |= {"Accept": "application/json"}
+
+The non-mutating operations return a ``CaseInsensitiveDict`` and leave their
+inputs unchanged. The in-place operation returns the same mapping object.
+When keys differ only by case, the right-hand value and spelling are used;
+existing key order is retained and new keys follow right-hand order.
+
 Eager to get started? This page gives a good introduction to Requests. It
 assumes you already have Requests installed. If not, head over to the
 :ref:`installation` section.
